     "result_text_tail": "ta. Please flip through it once in PowerPoint.\n- **Three charts aren't waterfalls.** The renderer draws waterfall bars wrong once the running total goes below zero. So the per-order breakdown, the plan-to-median bridge and the cash slide use bar charts with plus and minus values instead.\n- **Tables and number cards round to one decimal,** so the $1.99 delivery fee shows as $2.0. Exact values are in the sources workbook.\n\n**Choices I made without you**\n- A deep deck (30\u201360 slides), because this is a board decision, using only the briefing pack.\n- The audience is the board, deciding to approve or reject the launch; navy theme; ends with an action plan.\n- I read the $9.5M as covering all company spending to month 18, the reading kinder to the founders. Even then the plan breaks the runway rule. If it comes on top of today's burn, cash runs out before month 18; slide 21 shows both readings.\n- Contribution per order is shown before and after store fixed costs. The pack doesn't say how the incumbents define it, and a footnote says so.\n- Out of scope: a new funding round, other cities, and buying an incumbent. These are listed on the appendix slide of things not pursued.\n\nA useful next step would be to test the conclusion against the founders' month-by-month plan, if they have one; the pack doesn't include it. I can also switch the theme.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- parcelbird-now.pptx\n- parcelbird-now-sources.xlsx\n\nThe editable spec and the script that builds it are in `work/`."
    }
